index 0000000..7835791
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,63 @@
+# Helpdesk API
+
+Rails API-only backend for tenant-scoped helpdesk accounts. Set `DATABASE_URL` to a PostgreSQL connection URL, then run:
+
+```sh
+bundle install
+bin/rails db:prepare
+bin/rails server
+```
+
+All JSON endpoints use the `/api/v1` prefix. Requests after signup include `X-Helpdesk-Account: <subdomain>`, and authenticated requests include `Authorization: Bearer <session-token>`.
+
+## Account lifecycle
+
+1. `POST /api/v1/account/create` with `account.name`, `account.subdomain`, and `account.admin.name`, `email`, and `password`.
+2. `POST /api/v1/email_verifications/confirm` with `email_verification.token`.
+3. `POST /api/v1/sessions` with `session.email` and `session.password`.
+4. `GET/PATCH /api/v1/me`; `PUT /api/v1/me/password`.
+5. `POST /api/v1/account/cancel` and `/api/v1/account/reactivate` (owner only).
+
+Email and password reset link requests use `POST /api/v1/email_verifications` and `POST /api/v1/password_resets` with an `email` in the corresponding envelope. Confirm reset links at `/api/v1/password_resets/confirm` with `token` and `password`.
+
+`GET /api/v1/portal` is public for active accounts. `GET /api/v1/account` is authenticated.
+
+## Customer portal requests
+
+Customers register in an active portal with `POST /api/v1/registrations` and a `user` envelope containing `name`, `email`, and `password`. Registration uses the same verification email, login, profile, and password recovery endpoints as staff accounts.
+
+Authenticated customers create and manage their own requests at `POST /api/v1/requests` and `GET/PATCH /api/v1/requests/:id`. `GET /api/v1/requests/:id/comments` lists the conversation. Customers can filter their request list with `status`. Staff can read and update all account tickets through the corresponding `/tickets` endpoints. Request and ticket updates accept an optional `comment.body` and `status` in their resource envelope. Staff may also update ticket `priority` (`normal` or `high`); priority is omitted from customer responses and defaults to `normal`.
+
+List endpoints accept either legacy page numbers (`page` and `per_page`, defaults `1` and `25`) or cursor navigation (`page[size]`, then `page[after]` or `page[before]`). Legacy page-number responses retain `count`, `page`, `per_page`, `next_page`, and `previous_page`. All list responses include `meta.has_more`, `meta.after_cursor`, `meta.before_cursor`, and `links.next`/`links.prev`; links preserve the active filters. Requests and tickets are ordered by recent activity with ID tie-breaking, while comments are oldest first.
+
+Staff merge a duplicate with `POST /api/v1/tickets/:id/merge` and a `merge` envelope containing `target_id`. The source is closed and retains its comments while both staff and customer responses expose `merged_into_id` (or `null` when unmerged). The target must be an unclosed ticket for the same customer. Staff may override each private-by-default merge note with `source_comment` or `target_comment` containing `body` and `public`; merge notes never send email. Closed tickets remain readable and filterable but reject further edits and inbound replies. Later merges preserve earlier links as written.
+
+Staff ticket lists support combined `status`, `priority`, `assignee_id`, and `requester_id` filters plus a case-insensitive `q` search over ticket subjects and public comment text. Set `assignee_id=unassigned` to find tickets without an assignee. Search terms are matched literally, including `%`, `_`, and backslashes.
+
+## Team invitations and management
+
+Admins can create, list, inspect, resend, and revoke staff invitations at `/api/v1/invitations`. Pending invitations are single-use and block customer registration for the same normalized email. Invitation previews and acceptances are available at `/api/v1/invitation_previews` and `/api/v1/invitation_acceptances`; accepted invitees are verified immediately.
+
+Admins manage and filter users through `/api/v1/users`. Suspended staff lose all sessions and ticket assignments, and the last active admin cannot be suspended. Both admins and agents can use `/api/v1/staff` and update ticket `assignee_id`. Ticket comments accept `public: false` for staff-only private notes; customer request conversations omit those notes. The invitation, preview/acceptance, user, and staff routes are also available without the `/api/v1` prefix for frontend compatibility.
+
+Admins manage department groups and staff memberships through `/api/v1/groups` and `/api/v1/group_memberships`; all staff may browse both resources. Group and membership lists are ordered by ID and membership lists accept `group_id` and `user_id` filters. A staff member can belong to multiple groups, but has exactly one default while memberships remain. Use `PUT /api/v1/group_memberships/:id/make_default` to change it.
+
+Staff tickets expose `group_id` and the group's `id` and `name` in `group`. Ticket lists accept `group_id`, including `group_id=unassigned`. Assigning an ungrouped ticket to staff uses that person's default group when available. Group changes remove assignees who are no longer members, while clearing an assignee leaves the group unchanged and clearing the group clears the assignee. Suspension preserves group memberships.
+
+## Email support
+
+Action Mailbox accepts RFC 822 messages at `/rails/action_mailbox/relay/inbound_emails` with HTTP basic authentication (`actionmailbox` as the username and `RAILS_INBOUND_EMAIL_PASSWORD` as the password). Customers can send new requests to `<account-subdomain>@<HELPDESK_SUPPORT_DOMAIN>`; `HELPDESK_SUPPORT_DOMAIN` defaults to `support.example.test`. Cc recipients are considered when routing, and messages addressing multiple businesses are ignored.
+
+Email-created customers remain unverified and receive the normal portal verification link. Staff public replies to an email-created ticket are sent to the requester with that ticket's private `reply+...` address as the `From` and `Reply-To` address. Only that requester can add email replies through the private address, and a reply reopens pending or solved tickets but not closed tickets. Plain support-address messages always create new tickets.
+
+Messages are deduplicated by `Message-ID`; rejected or ignored messages do not reserve that ID. Automated responses and list mail are ignored.
+
+## Configuration
+
+- `DATABASE_URL`: PostgreSQL connection URL (required).
+- `HELPDESK_FRONTEND_URL`: frontend origin/base URL, default `http://localhost:3001`.
+- `HELPDESK_MAIL_FROM`: outgoing sender, default `support@example.test`.
+- `HELPDESK_SUPPORT_DOMAIN`: domain for tenant and private ticket reply addresses, default `support.example.test`.
+- `RAILS_INBOUND_EMAIL_PASSWORD`: password for the relay ingress (required when receiving mail).
+
+Run `bin/rails helpdesk:purge_cancelled_accounts` periodically to permanently remove accounts cancelled for at least 90 days.
